WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:01.857
- Hey man, I'm Kevin Smith!
- Jason Mewes!

00:00:01.857 --> 00:00:03.940
- And we play Jay and
Silent Bob and that's good

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.960
because this movie is called
"Jay and Silent Bob Reboot",

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.970
and it's coming out October 15th,

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.170
everywhere.
- Yes.

00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:12.450
- [Jay] We got three
days to get to Hollywood

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.000
and stop this reboot from ever happening.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.440
- Boys, I had a baby.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.900
Jay, brace yourself.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.883
You're about to meet our love child.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.053
- I think I'm gonna need
to see a blood test.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.248
- No, Jay, this is my
daughter Millennium Faulken.

00:00:29.248 --> 00:00:33.610
- Can you take us to Hollywood with you?

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.483
- No, man, it's a tough ass neighborhood.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.210
- Either you take us to Hollywood

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.240
or I stab you both to
death on my own front lawn.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.420
- And on that note, we cue the music.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.870
- I don't think the world needed another

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.750
Jay and Silent Bob movie but
we tried to make "Clerks 3"

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.842
and it didn't work 'cause
one of the cast members

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:51.675
didn't want to do it.

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:54.450
Then we tried to do "Mallrats
2" and that didn't work

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.210
cause Universal didn't want to do it.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.817
And so I was frustrated and I was like

00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.340
"You know, why are we banging
our heads against the wall".

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.280
We own "Jay and Silent Bob".

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.690
If I want to play with
my old toys so badly,

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.410
why don't we do it with
Jay and Silent Bob?

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.690
At least with "Reboot",
I put everything in it.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.500
I kind of encapsulated
my whole career, my life,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.680
his family's in it, his
whole family's in it.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.200
My whole family's in it and stuff.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.940
It's like a big scrapbook of a movie

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.550
but it is a gravestone of a movie.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.870
Essentially, look at the movie and like

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:20.840
here lies Kevin Smith,

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.370
it gives you everything you need to know

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.350
about who he was, when
he was born, when he died

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.320
and all that stuff
in-between is the good stuff.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.667
So, once we got the movie
done, then I was like

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.560
"All right, I feel better
about life, now I could die",

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.050
but I'm still here.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.490
- He's really clever in how he writes

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.330
to bring all the movies back.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.310
Like, you know, Jason Lee, you know

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.240
reading off the computer just
like Ben did in the last one

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.700
but different now instead of the internet.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.150
What's the internet, what's a Comic-Con,

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.741
it's, spoilers. (laughs)

00:01:51.741 --> 00:01:53.360
- You keep giving away the movie, man.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.675
- Sorry, sorry!

00:01:54.675 --> 00:01:56.816
It's super clever I feel.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.649
- Where were you?

00:01:57.649 --> 00:01:58.482
We could have used that on the poster.

00:01:58.482 --> 00:01:59.730
"Super clever, Jay Mewes".

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.563
- Exact.

00:02:00.563 --> 00:02:02.558
- "Super clever, the guy in the movie".

00:02:02.558 --> 00:02:05.188
(upbeat music)

00:02:05.188 --> 00:02:06.800
- Do I show them?
- Yeah.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.633
Pa-pazin!

00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:13.220
"Batman V Superman".

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.680
- Honestly, I've watched
this movie 30 times now

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.967
and I watch it every time,
you know my wife's like

00:02:17.967 --> 00:02:19.670
"Why you still watching that movie?"

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.060
'Cause I'm gonna love it one day.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.020
Should it have been made?

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:22.970
Let's go to you.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.150
- I feel like any movie, with one, for me

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.230
- Be careful, the internet
is listening and they're all

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:31.460
just sitting there waiting
to drag you, be careful.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.610
- It's something that
I've always wanted to see.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.737
Not necessarily that, but I always say

00:02:35.737 --> 00:02:37.067
"Hey, who could win in a fight?

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:40.220
"The Thing from Fantastic
Four or The Hulk?".

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.810
Or Superman, Batman,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:46.820
Superman, so for me to
get a ver, a V in there,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:50.360
I feel like, I was happy it was made.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.917
Not necessarily that movie--

00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:52.800
- You were waiting for
that V your whole life.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.206
- Yes, exactly.

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:55.039
- Like, put a V in every title, man.

00:02:55.039 --> 00:02:57.440
- That's it, I'm happy they made a V.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.330
Maybe not that movie, but
I'm happy they made a V.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.580
- More V's for you.
- V.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.418
- Batman, Batman, they
are rebooting Batman.

00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:08.251
- Yes.

00:03:08.251 --> 00:03:09.540
- And the boy from Twilight
is gonna be Batman now.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.750
He's gonna sparkle like
a vampire in Twilight.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.100
No, he's a genius actor
this kid, Rob Pattinson.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.500
He's gonna do a great job as Batman

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.650
and you should be happy.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.290
They're not getting some
like roided out dude

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.710
to play Batman, they're getting
little skinny kid like you.

