and then I was like "Well,
I'd watch that", you know.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.770
So maybe there's a way to
do it, don't reboot it,

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.627
you can't tell "The
Princess Bride" story again.

00:08:38.627 --> 00:08:39.687
That's a singular moment in time,

00:08:39.687 --> 00:08:41.290
that's like remaking "Clerks",

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.500
don't do that unless you call us,

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.363
and then keep us involved.

00:08:44.363 --> 00:08:45.890
- Do you feel like they
should redo the "Blade"?

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.220
- They are redoing "Blade".

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.630
- Without Wesley Snipes.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.730
- They are redoing, well,

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:50.960
I don't know that it will be without.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.329
Maybe they'll find a way to work him in,

00:08:52.329 --> 00:08:54.140
if Wesley wants to be involved,

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:57.070
but it won't be played
by Wesley this time.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.450
It will be Mahershala Ali.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.290
- Oh.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.767
- Yeah, he's coming back as "Blade".

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:02.600
- Oh, I like it.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.440
- He's gonna be "Blade".

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.640
- Oh no.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.750
- Spin it around.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.583
- Dun dun dun.

00:09:07.583 --> 00:09:08.910
- Now, they have rebooted this.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.330
The original series had a bunch of sequels

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:15.270
but then they rebooted it with
another guy fairly recently,

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.960
and they took all the humor out of it.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.793
- Yeah, I don't--

00:09:17.793 --> 00:09:19.347
- Like the first one was
kind of satirical and stuff

00:09:19.347 --> 00:09:20.910
"I'll buy that for a dollar!".

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.740
The reboot was just like,
they're like for reals man,

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:26.060
this cop is dead and now he's a robot, yo.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.040
Like it was very, very serious.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.570
Would you ever reboot "RoboCop"?

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:30.495
- No.

00:09:30.495 --> 00:09:31.328
- Why?

00:09:31.328 --> 00:09:32.161
- Because, I don't know.

00:09:32.161 --> 00:09:32.994
- What if they gonna write you a check?

00:09:32.994 --> 00:09:34.250
You didn't even ask how much!

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.350
You didn't ask any of
the pertinent questions.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:37.183
- Oh!

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.570
Say it three times.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:41.970
- Candyman.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:42.880
- Two more times--
- Candyman.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.713
- One more time.

00:09:43.713 --> 00:09:44.546
- Candyman.

00:09:44.546 --> 00:09:45.923
- Bullshit, bunch of bullshit.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:47.770
They're redoing this.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:51.090
They can redo this, I have no
skin in the "Candyman" game

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.890
where I'm like "What! That's a sacrilege".

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:54.310
It feels like you could totally redo this.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:57.210
In a world where they like
did a thousand "Halloween's",

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.727
then disavowed most of them, be like

00:09:58.727 --> 00:10:00.833
"Now the new ones are good",
they could totally get away--

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:01.900
- Was it done by Tony Todd?

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.100
Tony Todd did the first one?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:03.933
Was that who did it?

00:10:03.933 --> 00:10:05.716
- He was in it, he didn't
do it but he was the guy--

00:10:05.716 --> 00:10:07.050
- I mean, sorry, he was the
guy who played "Candyman".

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:08.190
- And he could totally come back--

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.023
- He could.

00:10:09.023 --> 00:10:10.430
- Or play another role in
it or something like that.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:12.730
- I see him as, "Tony Todd is Back".

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.810
- You want, but then it's not a reboot.

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:15.930
Then it's a sequel.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:16.763
- Is it?

00:10:16.763 --> 00:10:17.870
- If it's Tony Todd,
it's kind of a sequel.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.430
- Even if everything else is different?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.280
- Well, it could be a requel

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.563
which is a sequel with a reboot kind of--

00:10:22.563 --> 00:10:23.420
- Oh, right--

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:24.356
- Inside, they shove it inside.

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:25.347
- Oh, okay.

00:10:25.347 --> 00:10:26.490
- "Star Trek".

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:28.087
- Should they reboot
"Star Trek", they have!

00:10:28.087 --> 00:10:28.990
- "Star Trek".

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.750
- J.J. did it, did a really great job.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.200
- Yes.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.540
- Yeah, I like the new "Star Trek",

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:36.250
the old "Star Trek" I enjoy as well,

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.220
but a lot of thinking.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.220
A lot of sitting around and talking,

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.700
that's kind of like "Clerks" and stuff.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.710
J.J.'s "Star Trek" is like "Run Spock!",

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.489
like everybody's in a hurry and stuff.

00:10:44.489 --> 00:10:45.750
- And they have the technology now.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:46.900
- Yeah they can rebuild--

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:47.733
- For space.

00:10:47.733 --> 00:10:48.566
- Better, stronger, faster.

00:10:48.566 --> 00:10:49.513
- For space, ships.

00:10:49.513 --> 00:10:50.660
- Well, the first one
went to space as well.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.583
- But I'm saying now, they can
like actually make things--

00:10:52.583 --> 00:10:54.330
- Make it look better.

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:56.307
Like "That is the Final Frontier!".

00:10:56.307 --> 00:10:58.110
You didn't believe it when it was on TV?

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.902
You're like "That aint
space, it's a TV show,

00:11:00.902 --> 00:11:01.804
and that aint no Tribble".

00:11:01.804 --> 00:11:03.440
- Well, it was like tin
foil, and stuff like that.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.470
Now, it's like full on, you know.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.080
- Gene Roddenberry
rolling over in his grave

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.170
hearing you say tin foil.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:10.490
Crapping on an American icon.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.720
- Duck tape and tin foil!

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.327
- Oh my God!

00:11:13.327 --> 00:11:14.988
- "Po-poison!"

00:11:14.988 --> 00:11:16.780
- Whoa, whoa.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.613
- Now what?

00:11:17.613 --> 00:11:18.446
- Let me tell you something.

00:11:18.446 --> 00:11:20.030
- Well, here, let's discuss it.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.760
- All right, let's do it.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.630
- I think I could go
with this, here's why.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.003
You know, number one.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:27.380
Those are just two kids.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:28.213
- Yes.

00:11:28.213 --> 00:11:29.520
- There's a convenience store,

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.840
they have turnover and
employees all the time.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:33.920
You get all sorts of
clerks behind the counter.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.535
Number two, we're gonna
get a little taste,

00:11:36.535 --> 00:11:38.410
and do none of the work.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:39.260
None of the work!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.480
And, if the movie's good,
we'll get like credit

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:42.750
even though we didn't do anything.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:43.630
- Oh, I like it.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:45.550
- Yeah, work smarter not harder.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.413
That's what I say.

00:11:46.413 --> 00:11:47.246
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:11:47.246 --> 00:11:48.310
- Let me tell ya, if my kid got older

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.340
and wanted to reboot the movie,

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.240
that would be the best case scenario

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.960
because then I could
like shadow direct it.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:53.901
- Oh yeah.

00:11:53.901 --> 00:11:54.840
- From the sides and
stuff cause I'm her dad

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.020
I'm like "Oh no!", and stuff like that.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.450
- Yeah, yeah, no.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.870
- No, that'd be awesome,
like, that, how sweet.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.020
I hope to Lord, the Lord!

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:03.370
That my kid gets the idea.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.530
I should start planting that idea.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:05.363
- Yeah, yeah.

00:12:05.363 --> 00:12:06.440
- I'd be like "You should reboot Clerks".

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:07.920
- You should watch this episode.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.023
- Yeah, what episode?

00:12:09.023 --> 00:12:09.856
- What we're doing now.

00:12:09.856 --> 00:12:10.689
- Oh this!? Yeah.

00:12:10.689 --> 00:12:12.340
I'm like "Hey, you should watch
this thing on the internet"

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.077
and she's like "Is it you
and your friend again?

00:12:14.077 --> 00:12:14.980
"No way dad".

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.680
I'm like "Come on, this
one's interesting".

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:18.210
That could be our thing, man.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:21.580
Like the Smith thing, like how
Philip Morris has cigarettes.

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:24.530
We just have "Clerks" for the
rest of all time and stuff,

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:25.457
and people are like

00:12:25.457 --> 00:12:26.310
"Why are we still
watching this B.S. movie".

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.310
- Never forgotten.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:28.540
- Yeah, never.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.920
We could be in them too, we
get little cameos and stuff.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.497
As old men that come in
the store and be like--

00:12:32.497 --> 00:12:33.960
- (stutters)

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.940
- You could come in and be
like "Hey, where's the mall?"

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.517
and the audience would be like (claps).

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.940
Who else would you want
in a "Clerks" reboot?

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.600
- Playing Dante would be--

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:48.510
- Right now, I'd say, do
you ever watch "Fleabag"?

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.140
- Mm mm.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.110
- What's her name, Phoebe Waller-Bridge?

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:54.580
She's, that "Fleabag" is so good dude.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.610
I watched it before the Emmy's

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.610
so don't accuse me of being a bandwagon.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:58.556
- No, I--

00:12:58.556 --> 00:12:59.389
- That was big-time.

00:12:59.389 --> 00:13:01.940
I say, let her play both clerks.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:06.220
- All right and I say Thanos,
the guy who plays Thanos.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.053
- Oh wait--

00:13:07.053 --> 00:13:07.886
- And Vincent D'Onofrio--

00:13:07.886 --> 00:13:09.660
- The guy who plays
Thanos or Thanos himself.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:10.910
- No, the guy who plays Thanos.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:11.880
- So, Josh Brolin.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:12.796
- He is--

00:13:12.796 --> 00:13:13.690
- Cause I really want to see the version

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.810
of "Clerks" where Thanos is working there.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.730
Just because they serve you
doesn't mean they (snaps)

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.150
and everyone disappears and stuff.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.887
- We shouldn't have done that (snaps).

00:13:21.887 --> 00:13:23.333
- Listen to the editor.

